  "abstract": "JBoss Enterprise Web Server (JBEWS) is a fully integrated and certified set of\ncomponents for hosting Java web applications. It is comprised of the Apache HTTP\nServer, the Apache Tomcat Servlet container, Apache Tomcat Connector (mod_jk),\nJBoss HTTP Connector (mod_cluster), Hibernate, and the Tomcat Native library.\n\nThis enhancement update provides JBEWS 2.0 with improved capabilities on Red Hat\nEnterprise Linux 5. It aligns JBEWS with JBoss Enterprise Application Platform\n6, improves integration with Red Hat Enterprise Linux, and enhances JBEWS with a\nsubset of the frameworks of JBoss Web Framework 2.0. For detailed component and\ninstallation information refer to the Release Notes link in the References\nsection of this advisory. (BZ#848349)\n\nNote: Do not install JBEWS 2 on a host which has JBEWS 1 installed.\n\nAll users of JBoss Enterprise Web Server are advised to upgrade to these updated\nJBEWS packages.\n",
